<title>USA: Suffolk Bancorp proposes two-for-one split.</title>
<headline>Suffolk Bancorp proposes two-for-one split.</headline>
<dateline>RIVERHEAD, N.Y. 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Suffolk Bancorp said Monday that shareholders will vote on a two-for-one stock split at its annual meeting April 8.</p>
<p>If approved, shareholders of record May 1, will be entitled to their additional shares May 15.</p>
<p>The company said it believes a stock split wll improve the marketability of its common shares, putting it in reach of a wider range of investors.</p>
<p>The company maintain 25 offices in Suffolk County, Long Island, New York.</p>
